            <ArticleTitle>Bone Marrow Derived Eosinophil Cultures.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">e1161</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eosinophils are multifunctional effector cells implicated in the pathogenesis of a variety of diseases including asthma, eosinophil gastrointestinal disorders and helminth infection. Mouse bone marrow derived progenitor cells can be differentiated into eosinophils following IL-5 exposure. These bone marrow derived eosinophils are fully differentiated at the end of a 14 day culture based on morphology and expression of molecular markers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
